# ─── PUBLIC REPO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC. Anything ignored here is ignored because it must NOT be
# world-readable (solutions, the exam, student data) or because it is a build
# artifact. Solutions/exam live in the PRIVATE submodule `solutions/`.

# Quarto / render artifacts  (NOTE: _freeze/ is COMMITTED on purpose — see CLAUDE.md)
/_site/
_site/
.quarto/
*_cache/
*_files/

# LaTeX byproducts left next to .qmd
*.tex
*.log
*.aux
*.out

# R
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rapp.history
renv/library/

# Grading / feedback scratch (never commit student clones or PII)
/scratch/
/automation/ai-feedback/_work/
/automation/tracking/_work/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Student data — must never reach a public repo ───────────────────────────
# Commit only the header-only templates; keep filled copies as *.local.csv.
/tracking/students.local.csv
/tracking/attendance.local.csv
# Derived homework status lists student usernames — regenerate it, don't publish it.
/tracking/hw_status.csv
/tracking/progress.html
/tracking/progress_files/
# Week 1 survey responses. The real export is dropped in by hand as week01-survey.local.csv
# and overrides the committed week01-survey.csv, which holds test replies only. Never publish
# the local one: it holds free-text answers from a cohort of nine.
/website/slides/data/*.local.csv
# The cached brms fit embeds the responses it was fitted to, so it is student data as well.
/website/slides/data/*.rds
# Generated from week01.qmd by knitr::purl() before each session, so it is an artifact and
# never a source. See the deck's setup chunk.
/website/slides/week01-live.R

# _freeze/ is committed (it caches expensive model renders), but its site_libs/ subdir is
# 5+ MB of vendored JS that Quarto regenerates from its own install on every render.
/website/_freeze/site_libs/

notes.md